<title>USA: Fastenal makes executive changes.</title>
<headline>Fastenal makes executive changes.</headline>
<dateline>WINONA, Minn. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fastenal Co said effective immediately its corporate office will consist of four members, including president and chief executive officer Robert Kierlin and newly named vice president and chief operating officer Willard Oberton.</p>
<p>Rounding out the group are treasurer Daniel Florness who assumes the added titles of chief financial officer and chief accounting officer, and secretary Stephen Slaggie.</p>
<p>Fastenal said Kierlin previously held the titular title of CFO. It said Oberton, an operations manager, has been with the company for 18 years.</p>
<p>Fastenal manufactures specialty metal products.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
